    "extraction_notes": [
      "Ordering-code identity is preserved: the supplied MPN IRLML0030TRPBF corresponds to the datasheet spelling IRLML0030TRPbF, and p. 10 lists IRLML0030TRPbF as the orderable part number. The datasheet is branded International Rectifier; the manufacturer field follows the supplied Infineon Technologies metadata.",
      "The supplied PDF SHA-256 was verified as 19d848877ac1081b028c9e326d5441bc025c1e94fcf8df0e967a3cb5fb857135.",
      "Electrical characteristics are specified at TJ = 25 degC unless otherwise stated. Typical, minimum, and maximum meanings are preserved in source_kind.",
      "Output characteristics were digitized from selected 25 degC traces in p. 3 Fig. 1. The figure specifies pulse width <= 60 us. The 150 degC output traces were not extracted.",
      "The transfer characteristic was digitized from the 25 degC curve in p. 3 Fig. 3 at VDS = 15 V and pulse width <= 60 us. The 150 degC curve was not extracted.",
      "The capacitance curves were digitized from p. 4 Fig. 5. Both axes are logarithmic, with VGS = 0 V and f = 1 MHz. The table values at VDS = 15 V are retained in specs.",
      "Curve points are approximate manual reads at plotted grid intersections. No interpolated or model-derived points were added.",
      "The two published RDS(on) rows each have typical and maximum values at the same VGS and ID. They are represented as separate schema entries so the column semantics remain explicit.",
      "Additional published values not represented by dedicated schema fields include RG typ 2.3 ohm, gfs minimum 9.5 S at VDS = 10 V and ID = 5.2 A, Qg typ 2.6 nC, Qgs typ 0.8 nC, Qgd typ 1.1 nC, and switching times at the stated test conditions.",
      "Source-drain data include IS maximum 1.6 A, ISM maximum 21 A, VSD maximum 1.0 V, trr typical 11 ns and maximum 17 ns, and Qrr typical 4.0 nC and maximum 6.0 nC. The structured body_diode value is the published VSD maximum.",
      "IDSS is maximum 1 uA at VDS = 24 V and VGS = 0 V at TJ = 25 degC, and maximum 150 uA at the same bias at TJ = 125 degC.",
      "Thermal data provide RthetaJA maximum 100 K/W and a maximum 99 K/W condition for t < 10 s; no RthetaJC value is published. The normalized on-resistance and threshold-temperature figures were not extracted as structured curves."
    ],
